# Arrow functions

Prefer arrow functions wherever possible. This matches project ESLint (`prefer-arrow-callback`, `func-style`, `prefer-arrow/prefer-arrow-functions`).

```js
// ❌ BAD
function getRoomTemperature(req, res) { /* ... */ }
async function fetchHomey() { /* ... */ }
export default function registerRoutes(app) { /* ... */ }

// ✅ GOOD
const getRoomTemperature = async (req, res) => { /* ... */ };
const fetchHomey = async () => { /* ... */ };
export const registerRoutes = (app) => { /* ... */ };
```

Exceptions (do not force arrows):
- `class` methods and constructors
- Generator functions (`function*`)
- Cases where you need a non-lexical `this` or `arguments`
